 "how": "the seat's judgement, labelled as such by it: selection and the dictionary are one problem seen from two sides; choices removed on one side reappear on the other; what went wrong is the order of work (numbers before structure, averaging as a stand-in for 'no choice', forks priced late, a dictionary typed in); settle a choice only by equivalence or by consistency and count the rest; read where a symmetry fixes the point; run every rule on the rivals; make C^5 the Weil representation's own space. Not claims of fact. The note records itself what became of its two leads: the reading at tau = i was looked at and fails (W-L1, provisional; web-wl1-01), and the dictionary was sharpened and not closed (W-A2, main's B1952: one counted entry became four narrower ones). Its citations to the outside literature are not read at their source by main",
